"Set Trim Size, Bleed, and Margins (https://kdp.amazon.com/en_US/help/topic/GVBQ3CMEQW3W2VL6?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)\nciteturn14view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn13search0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 277\nL35:   * Account & Taxes\nL36:     * cite16†Set up your KDP account L37:       * cite17†Add or update a bank account L38:         * cite18†I set up my bank account, but I haven't received any payments. L39:         * cite19†Payment Service Provider Program Risk Management Controls L40:       * cite20†Verify your identity L41:         * cite21†What if my account name or country changes or is different from my ID? L42:     * cite22†Tax Information L43:       * cite23†Tax Withholding L44:         * cite24†Goods and Services Tax (GST) for eBooks in Australia and India L45:       * cite25†Applying for a US ITIN L46:         * cite26†Applying for a U.S. EIN for Corporations and Non-Individual Entities L47:   * KDP Publishing\nL48:     * cite27†Beta: Audiobooks with virtual voice L49:       * cite28†Audiobooks with virtual voice eligibility and troubleshooting L50:       * cite29†Terms and Conditions for the Beta Version of Audiobooks with Virtual Voice L51:     * cite30†Beta: Kindle Translate L52:       * cite31†Terms and Conditions for the Beta Version of Kindle Translate L53:   * Marketing & Distribution\nL54:     * cite32†Guidelines for use of the Available at Amazon Badge by KDP Publishers L55:   * User Guides\nL56:     * cite33†Kindle Publishing Guidelines L57:       * cite34†Guidelines for Specific Types of eBooks L58:         * cite35†Creating Fixed-Layout Books with Image Pop-Ups or Virtual Panels L59: ### Contact Us\nL60: \nL61: Have feedback? Can't find your answer in our Help pages?\nL62: \nL63: cite36†Contact Us L64: \nL65: [Input: Topic or Keyword]\nL66: \nL67: [Input] Search Help\nL68: \nL69: ## Set Trim Size, Bleed, and Margins\nL70: \nL71: This page details how to format your book's trim size and margins, depending on whether your book requires bleed, to ensure your book prints correctly. Without proper sizing, your manuscript may be rejected on upload, or you may see print quality issues with your printed book.\nL72: \nL73: * * *\nL74: ### Contents:\nL75: \nL76:   * cite37†Trim Size L77:   * cite38†Bleed L78:     * cite39†When to choose bleed for your interior L79:   * cite40†Margins L80:   * cite41†Formatting in Microsoft Word or Pages for Mac L81: \nL82: * * *\nL83: \nL84: A few key terms before you start:\nL85:   * Trim size. Your printed book's width and height. The most common trim size for books in the US is 6\" x 9\" (152.4 x 228.6 mm), but you have several other cite42†options . Books with a measurement more than 6.12 inches (155.5 mm) or more than 9 inches (228.6 mm) in height are considered large trim sizes.\nL86:   * Bleed. Bleed is a printing term that refers to when printed objects on a page, such as images, background color, or graphics, extend past where the publication will be trimmed. Setting your bleed properly ensures printed objects reach all the way to the edge of the page. Accounting for bleed is important, because it prevents a white border from appearing at the edge of the page when the book is trimmed.\nL87:   * Margins. Every page has three outside margins (top, bottom, and side) and one inside margin (also called the gutter). Margins ensure your text isn't cut off during manufacturing. Set your trim size before you set your margins, since margin size depends on page count and on whether you have elements that bleed.\nL88: * * *\nL89: ### Trim Size\nL90: cite43†iframe†www.youtube.com L91: You can choose from a variety of trim sizes to set the size of your printed book. The most common trim size for paperbacks in the U.S. is 6 x 9 inches (152.4 x 228.6 mm) and is a regular trim size. The size of your book will determine its page count, and there are minimum and maximum page counts by size, which are listed in the cite42†Trim Size Specifications table below.\nL92: Books with a measurement more than 6.12 inches (155.5 mm) in width or more than 9 inches (228.6 mm) in height are considered large trim sizes and have different printing costs than regular trim sizes. Learn more about printing costs for cite44†paperback and cite45†hardcover books.\nL93: Note: To set your trim size, you typically need to adjust the page or paper size setting in your chosen software (for example, Microsoft Word).\nL94: You can cite46†download a Microsoft Word template in the trim size you need with or without sample content.\nL95: Trim size specifications (width x height) with minimum and maximum page counts(kdp.amazon.com)\nL96:   Paperback\nL97: Trim Size  | Black ink and white paper  | Black ink and cream paper  | Black ink and groundwood paper  | Standard color ink and white paper  | Premium color ink and white paper\nL98: 5\" x 8\" (12.7 x 20.32 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL99: 5.06\" x 7.81\" (12.85 x 19.84 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL100: 5.25\" x 8\" (13.34 x 20.32 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL101: 5.5\" x 8.5\" (13.97 x 21.59 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL102: 6\" x 9\" (15.24 x 22.86 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL103: Large Trim Sizes\nL104: 6.14\" x 9.21\" (15.6 x 23.39 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL105: 6.69\" x 9.61\" (16.99 x 24.41 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL106: 7\" x 10\" x (17.78 x 25.4 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL107: 7.44\" x 9.69\" (18.9 x 24.61 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 24 - 812  | 72 - 600  | 24 - 828\nL108: 7.5\" x 9.25\" (19.05 x 23.5 cm)  | 24 - 828  | 24 - 776  | 2